# ACT III, optional: the far salt pans, as the last of the fog comes off the lagoon. No puzzle and
# nothing needed: a barrel, a view of the Arcadia, and the talk a father and son never had room
# for (dialogue/pans.adv). Reached from the salt camp once Ansel has handed over flag sixteen,
# by the far pans at the camp's left edge or by asking him where he goes to think (ansel.adv).
# Ansel comes down with Fenn and walks back up with him: arriving here sets ansel_out, arriving
# in the camp clears it, and each room shows him only on its own side of that flag.
room far_pans "Gullet Key — the Far Pans"
  bg bg_farpans_wide
  width 2560
  music music_pans
  ambience wind
  perspective horizon 270 ref 875 height 340
  # The bank of packed salt along the front. The pans behind it are water, not floor.
  walk (40,878) (62,810) (2498,810) (2528,878)
  entry 2380,846

  footsteps sand
  water (590,560) (820,560) (820,630) (590,630) ripple 1.4
  water (960,545) (1320,545) (1320,635) (960,635) ripple 1.4
  water (1990,600) (2240,600) (2240,685) (1990,685) ripple 1.4
  motes glints (590,565) (820,565) (820,625) (590,625) count 20
  motes glints (960,550) (1320,550) (1320,630) (960,630) count 25
  motes glints (1990,605) (2240,605) (2240,680) (1990,680) count 15
  haze 245 380 floor 400 alpha 0.12 speed 6 tint "#e6e1d8"
  emit lapping at 900,700

  # On his barrel at the edge of the pans, facing along the bank toward the camp.
  sprite npc_ansel_seated at 740,846 size 0.85 idle speaker ansel for ansel grade "saturate(0.9) brightness(0.98) sepia(0.06)"

  on enter
    set ansel_out

  scene if not pans_seen
    set pans_seen
    say "My father comes down to the far pans with me. He settles on an upturned barrel, the way other men settle into a chair."

  hotspot sky "the sky"
    area 0,0 2560x235
    nowalk
    look "A sky the colour of the inside of a shell. In Port Vela the sky is mostly the colour of the customs house."

  hotspot pans "the pans"
    area 0,380 2560x412
    nowalk
    look "Flooded pans, flat as glass, each one holding its own copy of the sky. Three years of salt, and the first thing here Cray can't sell."

  hotspot fog "the lifting fog"
    area 560,236 1000x130
    nowalk
    look "The last of Cray's fog, coming off the lagoon in long white sheets, like a bill being torn up very slowly."

  hotspot wreck "the Arcadia"
    area 1075,35 290x300
    nowalk
    look "The Arcadia, small on the reef from here, heeled over with both masts up. From this far she looks as if she's only stopped to listen."

  hotspot boardwalk "the boardwalk"
    area 0,345 845x245
    stand 430,846
    look "A boardwalk on stilts, running out across the pans toward the lagoon and stopping a few yards short, as if it lost its nerve."
    walk "It goes out over the water and stops. I've had afternoons like that."

  hotspot rakes "the rakes"
    area 825,660 225x140
    nowalk
    look "Salt rakes, dropped where they stood. Nobody's raking now. Word has gone round the camp faster than Pike can count it."

  hotspot heron "the heron"
    area 852,525 88x132
    nowalk
    look "A heron, standing on one leg in a salt pan with the air of a magistrate who has heard every excuse, including mine."

  hotspot salt "the salt heap"
    area 1690,628 285x118
    nowalk
    look "Salt, raked into a heap and left to dry. Somebody has drawn a face in it with a finger. It isn't a good face, but it's had three years too."

  hotspot gull "the gull"
    area 1792,582 100x62
    nowalk
    look "A gull on top of the salt heap, surveying the view on behalf of the management."

  hotspot camp "the salt camp"
    area (1985,185) (2560,165) (2560,800) (2380,800) (1960,470)
    stand 2470,846
    exit salt_camp sound none
    look "The camp, back along the shore. Tents, washing, and a hundred and thirty sailors who are still getting used to the idea."

  # Last, so he wins over the pans and the rakes behind him.
  hotspot ansel "Ansel Fenn"
    show if ansel_out
    area 630,575 240x275
    stand 975,846
    look "My father on his barrel, looking out at his ship. He sits like a man who has had three years to get a barrel exactly right."
    talk "He shuffles along the barrel to make room. There isn't any. He does it anyway."
      talk pans
    give "“Unless it's a second barrel, son, hang on to it.”"
    state if seen:pans.root
      talk "He pats the barrel beside him, where there still isn't any room."
        talk pans at again

  use flag16 on ansel
    "He closes my hands round it. “Not to me, son. Up the Arcadia's mast. I'll be watching. I've had the practice.”"
  use flag16 on wreck
    "From here I'd need an arm a mile long. Across the flats from the camp, then, and up her halyard."
  use compass on ansel
    "He taps the glass. “Your grandfather made it. I sailed by it. You carried it here in a customs coat. It's had a confusing life.”"
  use compass on wreck
    "The needle swings past the Arcadia and settles beyond the reef, on the Old Nail. It never did love her the way he does."
  use ansel_log on ansel
    "He won't take it back. “Keep it. That last page was a letter I had nowhere to post. It reached the right family in the end.”"
  use stamp on ansel
    "He holds out his wrist like a man at a dance. I stamp it: HARBOUR OF PORT VELA. “Nearly home, then,” he says, and doesn't rub it off."
